course: dictionary
lesson: 12442
title: Declared: said clearly and officially
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Declared is the past form of declare. When someone declares something, they say it clearly, firmly or officially, so everyone knows. «The referee declared the match a draw.» The referee did not just guess. The words declared the match a draw show an official decision.
explain: Use the words around it to find the meaning. «The school declared the library open on Monday.» The library opened after an official announcement, so declared means announced officially. Check it: swap in said clearly and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: As an adjective, declared means stated publicly or openly. «Mia is the declared winner of the spelling bee.» Everyone has been told officially, so there is no doubt. A declared aim is one that a person says out loud for everyone to hear.
fact: Declared is the past form of declare: declare, declares, declared, declaring.
fact: «Declared» means said clearly, firmly or officially.
fact: As an adjective, «declared» means stated publicly or openly, as in «a declared aim».
fact: In sport and games, a declared winner is the official winner.
fact: Phrases to know: declared war, declared independence, declared open.
exercise: «The judge declared the painting a fake.» What does declared mean? | Painted again | Hid carefully | Lost quietly | *Said officially
exercise: «She declared her aim: to swim across the lake.» What is a declared aim? | A lost aim | *An aim that is stated openly | A secret aim | A broken aim
exercise: «The declared winner ran up to the stage.» What does declared mean here? | Hidden | *Officially named | Very loud | Very tired
test: «The king declared war, and the army marched out.» What does declared mean? | *Officially announced | Whispered softly | Quietly forgotten | Covered up
test: Sam says, «My declared favourite is pizza.» What does declared suggest? | A secret favourite | A favourite that is lost | *A favourite stated openly | A favourite that is broken
exam: «The mayor declared the new bridge open, and everyone cheered.» What does declared open show? | *An official opening was announced | The bridge fell down | The bridge was painted | Nobody knew about it
